@startuml needs_block_rule
' "Needs a block" part 1 — the pure brain and the two clocks.
' See docs/design-addendum-needs-a-block.md. Self-contained style:
' _style.puml is referenced by quickadd_flow.puml but missing from the
' repo (flagged in the addendum §H) — this diagram carries its own.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #616974
  FontColor #272C33
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EDF4F1
  BorderColor #2F7E6E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FBF3E4
  BorderColor #DD9B4A
}
title "Needs a block" — one pure rule, one derived list, two clocks (v21.5, parts 1–3)

database "AppData\n(tasks + events)" as AD
rectangle "bounded scan (§F)\nONE pass over events:\ntask-linked, dated **today or later**,\nbucketed by taskId" as SCAN #EDF4F1

rectangle "coverage::isCovered (pure, §A)\nblock date in [today, deadline]\ndeadline = **max(due, today)**\npast blocks never count\nlate blocks never count" as COV

rectangle "coverage::needsBlock (pure, §B)\nopen? not dismissed (until > now)?\nnot covered?\n**priority in flag set** OR\noverdue OR **due within window**" as NB

rectangle "coverage::rung (pure, §D)\nDERIVED from dismissCount:\n0 ordinary / 1 decision / 2 pinned\nnever stored" as RUNG

rectangle "AppData::tasksNeedingBlock\nTHE derived list — every surface\nrenders this one query\nsorted: pinned, overdue, urgent, rest" as LIST #EDF4F1

rectangle "coverage::uncoveredReason (§A)\nfull history, flagged tasks only:\nNoBlock / BlockAfterDeadline /\nBlockInPast — the owed \"why\"" as WHY

rectangle "ReturnPolicy (pure, §C)\nEndOfDay / AtTime / AfterHours\none nextReturn(from), used twice" as RP
rectangle "review clock\nprefs:: · default 06:00" as RC #FBF3E4
rectangle "PLACEMENT (part 3)\nFind time -> placing mode:\nday strip + highlight runs;\nintercepted at planAt — the ONE\nplanning step, so week view\nworks for free" as PLACE
rectangle "THE GATE (part 2)\nNeedsBlockCard in GlancePanel\n**open = nextReturn(lastReview) > now**\nlastReview: QSettings, per-DEVICE\nno stored open/closed flag" as GATE
rectangle "dismissal clock\nprefs:: · default 21:00\n\"while I plan tomorrow\"" as DC #FBF3E4

rectangle "doors (AppData, §C/§D)\ndismissTask(id, until) — counts++\nclearDismissal — count stays\nexpireDismissals(now) — housekeeping\nsetTaskDone(true) — **resets evidence**" as DOORS

AD --> SCAN
SCAN --> COV
COV --> NB : covered?
NB --> LIST
RUNG --> LIST : ordering
LIST ..> WHY : per flagged task,\non demand
RP --> RC
RP --> DC
RC --> GATE : the third consumer —\nzero new code
LIST --> GATE : card / strip / clear
GATE ..> PLACE : "Find time"
PLACE --> AD : addTaskEvent\n(the existing door)
DC ..> DOORS : computes `until`;\nthe domain stores the FACT
DOORS --> AD

note bottom of NB
  pure functions of their arguments —
  no widget, no QSettings, no clock.
  the glance panel (part 2) and the
  week view (part 3) cannot drift,
  because there is nothing to copy.
end note

note bottom of DC
  two clocks, deliberately independent:
  dismissal = defer to a better moment,
  not "shut up until morning".
end note
@enduml
